Title: 2.2.10: Flowable do not use correct scheduler once bufferSize is reached
Description: Hi, I was playing with Flowable to get a deep understanding on how to handle backpressure without dropping events and running the following code I noticed that the flowable starts to emit events on the subscriber scheduler once bufferSize given to observeOn method is reached.

Here's the code :

```
    public static void main(String[] args) throws InterruptedException {
        int maxI = 12;
        int bufferSize = 5;
        CountDownLatch waitForIt = new CountDownLatch(1);
        CompositeDisposable compositeDisposable = new CompositeDisposable();

        Flowable<Integer> integerFlow = Flowable.<Integer, Integer>generate(
                () -> 0,
                (i, emitter) -> {
                    if (i < maxI) {
                        log("Emitting: " + i);
                        emitter.onNext(i);
                    } else {
                        emitter.onComplete();
                    }
                    return i + 1;
                }).observeOn(Schedulers.io(), false, bufferSize);

        compositeDisposable.add(
                integerFlow
                        .subscribeOn(Schedulers.computation())
                        .subscribeWith(new DisposableSubscriber<Integer>() {

                            @Override
                            public void onNext(Integer i) {
                                try {
                                    log("Receiving: " + i);
                                    Thread.sleep(10L);
                                } catch (InterruptedException e) {
                                    e.printStackTrace();
                                }
                            }

                            @Override
                            public void onError(Throwable throwable) {

                            }

                            @Override
                            public void onComplete() {
                                compositeDisposable.remove(this);
                                waitForIt.countDown();
                            }
                        }));

        System.out.println(compositeDisposable.size());
        log("Waiting for finish");
        waitForIt.await();
        System.out.println(compositeDisposable.size());
    }

    private static void log(String message) {
        System.out.println(message + String.format(" (%s)", Thread.currentThread().getName()));
    }
```
